    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We can see that $5^1 = 5,$\n$5^2 = 25,$\n$5^3 = 125,$\nand so on. In general, $5^n = 125$ when $n$ is a multiple of $3.$\nTherefore, the rightmost three digits of $5^{1993}$ is the same as the rightmost three digits of $5^3$\nwhich is $\\boxed{125}$.The answer is: 125",
