    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "First, we compute the powers of $5$ to find a pattern.\n\\begin{align*}\n5^1 &\\equiv 5 \\pmod{1000} \\\\\n5^2 &\\equiv 25 \\pmod{1000} \\\\\n5^3 &\\equiv 125 \\pmod{1000} \\\\\n5^4 &\\equiv 625 \\pmod{1000} \\\\\n5^5 &\\equiv 3125 \\equiv 125 \\pmod{1000} \\\\\n5^6 &\\equiv 625 \\pmod{1000} \\\\\n\\end{align*}\nIt appears that the rightmost three digits of $5^n$ repeat every four powers of $5$.\nTherefore, to find the rightmost three digits of $5^{1993}$, we need to determine the value of $1993$ modulo $4$.\nSince $1993 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}$, the rightmost three digits of $5^{1993}$ are the same as the rightmost three digits of $5^1$.\nTherefore, the rightmost three digits of $5^{1993}$ are $\\boxed{062}$.The answer is: 062",
